This is a common beginner confusion.

### Database

The **data itself**.

```text
Database
├── students
├── courses
└── results
```

### RDBMS

The **software that manages the database**.

```text
PostgreSQL
      ↓
manages
      ↓
Database
```

### Simple analogy

Think:

```text
Library
   ↓
Books = Database
Librarian/System = RDBMS
```

### 🎤 Interview Answer

> A database is a collection of stored data, while an RDBMS is the software used to create, manage, query, and control that data. PostgreSQL is an example of an RDBMS.

